      "title": "TT-104: Undo task operations",
      "brief": "Implement TT-104 from BACKLOG.md exactly.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Add TaskStore.undo() for the most recent not-yet-undone successful add, complete, or delete; repeated calls traverse history in LIFO order across operation kinds.\n- Undo add removes that task; undo complete reopens it; undo delete restores the task exactly under the same id.\n- Ids are never reused, including after undoing an add.\n- With no remaining operation to undo, raise tasktracker.store.NothingToUndo (define it there).\n- Failed operations, such as completing an unknown id, are not recorded.\n- Add focused tests for all operation kinds, combined LIFO history, ID allocation, and failed operations. Use only Python standard library.\n- Keep existing tests passing with: python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .\n- Commit this ticket's implementation and tests as its own separate commit.",
